    "created_at": "2024-04-02T02:58:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-04-02T02:58:25Z",
    "body": "I looked into this a bit thanks to your comment. Apparently HTMLMetaElement can ([or at least once could](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/b36775ffedb1f9465f9ae112bacbcad96b35e4e7)) run script synchronously, which is absolutely not allowed during the normal insertion steps, so its entire processing phase got relegated to the post-insertion steps.\r\n\r\nAssuming it still can run script synchronously for some meta types, I kind of imagine we could technically pull the non-script-running types into the \"insertion steps\", and keep only the script-running-types in the \"post-insertion steps\" but I'm not sure that buys us very much and it would require Blink & WebKit to change their longstanding behavior with probably very little upside for the vendors, so I'm not sure it's worth it.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/2030984510/reactions",
